--- a/docs/USAGE.md
+++ b/docs/USAGE.md
-ta cleanup --only drafts,staging     # Limit to: drafts, staging, goals, locks, archive
+ta cleanup --only drafts,staging     # Limit to: drafts, staging, goals, locks, archive, branches
+prune_branches = true # Delete finished local branches and their clean worktrees (default on)
+
+### Pruning finished branches and worktrees
+
+Branches and worktrees whose work has merged are removed without you asking. Cleanup decides from the pull request state reported by your VCS adapter, not from `git branch -d` or `git cherry`, because a squash merge rewrites commits and makes a finished branch look unmerged to both.
+
+A local branch is deleted automatically when either:
+
+- its pull request is merged and the branch has no commits beyond the head commit recorded for that PR, or
+- its tip is already an ancestor of the default branch.
+
+If a clean worktree has the branch checked out, the worktree is removed first. Everything else is a question and is never deleted for you: a branch with an open PR, with no recorded PR, with commits beyond the PR head, or in a worktree that has uncommitted or untracked files (the question lists the files). The current branch and the default branch are never touched.
+
+```bash
+ta cleanup --only branches --dry-run   # Show each branch, the evidence and the reason
+ta cleanup --only branches             # Delete the finished ones, ask about the rest
+```
+
+Every deletion is logged in `.ta/audit.jsonl` and `.ta/cleanup/pruned-branches.jsonl` with the branch name and its tip commit. To bring a branch back:
+
+```bash
+git branch <name> <tip-sha>
+```
+
+This runs on its own after `ta draft watch` (or `ta draft apply --watch`) sees the PR merge, and in the daemon's scheduled cleanup, even when `auto = "off"`. Set `prune_branches = false` under `[cleanup]` to turn it off.
+
+Remote branches are never deleted by cleanup (let your host delete head branches on merge). A remote branch whose PR was closed without merging is listed in the report with the `git push origin --delete <name>` command to run yourself.
